                <pb facs="0342" n="228" xml:id="pg228"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2300/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Prince</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-08-01T17:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1,
                                1923—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 1—1:53
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>26. Department’s telegram 20, July 17, 2 p.m. Danish Foreign Office informs me
                    that Icelandic Government has granted permission for proposed investigation by
                    War Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Prince</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
